Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='versionreading', at=datetime(2026, 10, 12, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='The version is a reading of the project chain: a release is a todo whose spec composes its items', body="*THE VERSION IS A READING OF THE PROJECT CHAIN* (the owner, 2026-10-12; plain feature releases since 2026-10-23; `suzatary_core::release`). A release is a todo on the `suzatary` chain whose spec composes its items (`Ref`s), declared in order in `app/core/releases.toml` with its own `major` and `minor`: `suzatarytwo` is 2.0, `suzatarytwoone` 2.1, `suzatarytwotwo` 2.2, `suzatarytwothree` 2.3. A plan whose versions do not strictly increase is refused (`Plan::new`). MAJOR.MINOR is the last completed release's (`base`.0 before any); PATCH counts the trains since that MAJOR.MINOR was first tagged, from origin/master's newest `Release:` trailer. Items show a release's progress and move no version; `release read` lists them with what became of each. `Reading::of` is the one rule, a join over the SET of objects: completed once is completed, so a reopened release stays shipped (`app/core/tests/release.rs` pins it the last completed release's, monotone and a function of the set). The tags up to 2.1.2 were read while items counted toward MINOR. A PR names what it completes on `Completes:` lines of its description (AGENTS.md); `scripts/train.sh` checks each id at `build` and cuts the release there (so the gate judges it), and at `land` asks `suzatary release check` whether the chain with those todos done reads at least that version, pushes master and `v<version>` in one atomic push, and only then records each done as `assistant` naming the PR. Every train command first fetches origin's master and tags and records origin's newest release (`suzatary release record`, idempotent; `train.sh record` by hand), so a failed record is repaired by the next command; the last release is origin/master's newest `Release:` trailer, its one reader; the binary that writes the chain is built from a named commit (origin/master, or the train at land; `SUZATARY_APP_REV` to `scripts/app-bin.sh`), never the checkout as it is; and `train.sh record <rev>` refuses a rev off origin/master's first-parent chain. `suzatary release items <release> --add|--remove` rescopes a release in one revision; an item moved out stays listed, as dropped. So the tag, the changelog, `app/release.toml` (the version and the IDS of what it completed, never a title, since the file is public; `/api/about` and Settings read titles off the chain) and the chain say one thing, and a refused push writes nothing.", rationale='The owner, 2026-10-12; plain feature releases since 2026-10-23. The tags up to 2.1.2 were read while items counted toward MINOR.', supersedes=()))